UPDATE companies SET description='Value Plus Auto Parts Wholesale operates from two locations in the Detroit metro area — Westland and Detroit, Michigan — and has served Southeast Michigan since its founding in 1997. The business was established as a wholesale auto parts supplier focused on repair facilities, commercial auto businesses, and retail customers, building a reputation for dependable service and competitive pricing over more than two decades.

The company distributes a broad range of automotive components including brake parts, ignition components, engine parts, cooling system parts, suspension parts, filters, electrical components, and motor oil for both domestic and import vehicles.

Primary customers are independent repair shops, commercial fleet operators, and retail motorists throughout Southeast Michigan. The supplier also works with independent mechanics and automotive service centers that rely on quick access to quality parts from brands such as Bosch, Denso, Dorman, AC Delco, Timken, TRW, and Hitachi.

Value Plus differentiates itself through a mission to provide quality parts at the most competitive prices by leveraging a network of small businesses that negotiate collectively with vendors. Its promise emphasizes availability, service programs for both retail and repair facilities, and a commitment to longevity through prosperity, backed by knowledgeable staff and a professional, organized operation.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Wholesale distribution of automotive parts", "Fast delivery", "Stocking accounts", "Large inventory coverage (good, better, best tiers)", "Domestic and import vehicle parts coverage", "Competitive wholesale pricing", "Auto Center Program", "Online ordering and forms", "Delivery tracking", "Nationwide warranty program (APA PRO Auto Care)"], "industries": ["Automotive repair shops", "Commercial auto businesses", "Retail automotive customers"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Fast delivery and delivery tracking for repair facilities and commercial customers", "Stocking accounts and competitive wholesale pricing", "Online ordering and forms for repair shops", "APA PRO Auto Care nationwide warranty program"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1997, serves Southeast Michigan -> /", "Two locations: Detroit (8121 Livernois Ave) and Westland (1021 Manufacturers Dr) -> /", "Distributes brake, ignition, engine, cooling, suspension, filters, electrical, motor oil for domestic/import -> /", "Offers fast delivery, stocking accounts, online ordering, delivery tracking, warranty program -> /", "Serves repair facilities, commercial auto businesses, retail customers -> /", "Mission: quality parts at competitive prices via small business network -> /about-us", "Promise: good/better/best tiers, availability, programs for retail and repair -> /about-us", "Brands carried: Bosch, Denso, Dorman, AC Delco, Timken, TRW, Hitachi -> /"], "company_type": "Distributor / reseller", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Value Plus Auto Parts Wholesale has been a trusted wholesale auto parts supplier serving repair facilities, commercial auto businesses, and retail customers across Southeast Michigan.", "founded_year": "1997", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='value-plus-auto-parts-wholesale' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='VanTran Transformers was founded in 1963 in Vandalia, Illinois, and relocated to Waco, Texas in 1974, where it remains headquartered and operates its manufacturing facility. The company is now part of the Forgent power infrastructure group, which combines VanTran with MGM Transformers, States Manufacturing, and PwrQ to deliver end-to-end power solutions.

VanTran designs and manufactures custom distribution-class transformers, including padmount, substation, multi-tap substation, auto-transformers, submersible and vault, grounding, polemount, and dry medium-voltage units (VPI and cast resin). Its capabilities span custom engineering, retrofit design solutions, and in-house manufacturing, supported by a workforce of 51 to 200 employees.

The company serves industrial, oil and gas, petrochemical, utility, data center, rental power, renewable energy, mining, and transit markets. Customers include data centers, manufacturing facilities, and power-grid operators requiring short delivery cycles and on-time delivery for critical infrastructure projects.

VanTran emphasizes timely, customizable, liquid-filled distribution transformers with what it describes as the shortest lead times in the industry. The firm has been recognized on the Inc. 5000 list of fastest-growing U.S. companies, citing exponential growth that enables expanded client support while maintaining high-quality standards.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom engineering", "Retrofit design solutions", "In-house manufacturing"], "industries": ["Industrial", "Oil and gas", "Petrochemical", "Utility", "Data centers", "Rental power", "Renewable energy", "Mining", "Transit", "Transportation"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Shortest lead times in the industry", "Customizable liquid-filled distribution transformers with short delivery cycles", "Over 50 years of transformer manufacturing experience", "Inc. 5000 recognized fastest-growing company", "Backed by Forgent''s full power infrastructure portfolio"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1963 in Vandalia, IL -> /about-us", "Relocated to Waco, TX in 1974 -> /about-us", "Headquartered and manufacturing in Waco, Texas -> db", "Part of Forgent power infrastructure group -> db, /", "Employee count 51-200 -> db", "Products: padmount, substation, multi-tap substation, auto-transformers, submersible/vault, grounding, polemount, dry medium voltage (VPI and cast resin) -> db, /", "Capabilities: custom engineering, retrofit design solutions, in-house manufacturing -> db", "Industries served: industrial, oil and gas, petrochemical, utility, data centers, rental power, renewable energy, mining, transit -> db, /", "Shortest lead times in the industry -> /", "Inc. 5000 fastest-growing company -> /", "Timely, customizable, out-of-the-box liquid filled distribution class transformers -> /about-us", "LinkedIn URL -> db"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Custom distribution-class transformer manufacturer headquartered and manufacturing in Waco, Texas", "founded_year": "1963", "employee_count": "51-200", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": ["https://www.linkedin.com/company/vantranxfmr"], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='vantran-transformers' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Vanguard Manufacturing operates from a 101,100-square-foot facility on nine acres in New Ipswich, New Hampshire. The company became part of the Lyn-Lad Group in 1970 when Lynn Ladder founder Bernard "Bernie" Kline acquired it, and it remains family owned and operated today.

The company manufactures a full line of steel frame scaffolding, fixed steel access ladders, steel roof ladders, a proprietary chimney bracket scaffold, aluminum planks and stages, and rugged truck and van racks. Since the late 1970s it has applied an electrostatic powder coat finish that became an industry standard for durability. In addition to manufacturing, Vanguard runs an extensive rental division that supplies frame scaffold, planks, and Hydro Mobile mast climbers to job sites across the country. Custom fabrication is offered with short lead times because production is kept in house.', certifications=ARRAY['Women Owned Business','Commonwealth of Massachusetts Certification']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Steel frame scaffold manufacturing", "Fixed steel access ladder manufacturing", "Steel roof ladder manufacturing", "Chimney bracket scaffold manufacturing", "Aluminum plank and stage manufacturing", "Truck and van rack manufacturing", "Electrostatic powder coating", "Custom fabrication", "Scaffold rental", "Mast climber rental"], "industries": ["Construction", "Industrial maintenance", "Commercial contracting", "Equipment rental"], "materials": ["Steel", "Aluminum"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Electrostatic powder coat finish established as industry standard in late 1970s", "Custom sizes with quick turnaround due to in-house manufacturing", "Extensive scaffold rental division including Hydro Mobile mast climbers", "Family owned and operated since 1970 acquisition", "Women owned business certified in Massachusetts"], "facts_used": ["101,100 sq ft facility on 9 acres in New Ipswich, NH -> /about", "Joined Lyn-Lad Group in 1970, acquired by Bernard \"Bernie\" Kline -> /about", "Family owned and operated -> /about", "Manufactures steel frame scaffold, fixed steel access ladders, steel roof ladders, chimney bracket scaffold, aluminum planks and stages, truck and van racks -> /about", "Electrostatic powder