UPDATE companies SET description='Vapor Apparel is based in Hanahan, South Carolina, and was founded in 2008. The company operates as a manufacturer of sun-protective performance apparel.

The company produces a range of UPF 50+ rated shirts, hoodies, base layers, and midweight polos for men and women. Its product lines include the Solar series, midweight fabrics designed for layering, and a print shop offering custom graphics on stock garments. Vapor Apparel also runs a wholesale division supplying retailers and bulk buyers.

The brand targets outdoor enthusiasts in fishing, hunting, coastal, and general sun-protection markets.

Vapor Apparel emphasizes its proprietary SolarBloc® technology, which provides permanent UPF 50+ protection combined with moisture-wicking and stretch properties. The company also highlights a partnership with the Skin Cancer Foundation, underscoring its focus on sun safety.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Apparel manufacturing", "UPF 50+ fabric development", "Custom printing (print shop)", "Wholesale distribution", "E-commerce retail"], "industries": ["Outdoor recreation", "Fishing", "Hunting", "Coastal lifestyle", "Sun protection apparel", "Wholesale textile"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Proprietary SolarBloc\u00ae UPF 50+ sun protection", "Moisture-wicking, stretch midweight fabrics", "In-house print shop for custom graphics", "Wholesale program for retailers and bulk buyers"], "facts_used": ["Founded 2008 -> db", "Headquarters Hanahan, SC -> db", "Products: sun protection clothing, UPF 50+ performance shirts -> /", "Wholesale program -> /", "Print shop with custom graphics -> /", "Categories: Coastal, Hunting + Outdoors, Fishing, USA + State, Base Layers -> /", "SolarBloc\u00ae UPF 50+ technology -> /", "Skin Cancer Foundation partnership -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Vapor Apparel | Sun Protection Clothing | UPF 50+ | Performance Shirts", "founded_year": "2008", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='vapor-apparel' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Vaso Corporation, formerly Vasomedical, Inc., is headquartered in Plainview, New York, with additional operations in Wuxi, China; Nashville, Tennessee; and Tampa, Florida. The public company operates across healthcare and information technology through three business units.

The VasoMedical unit designs, manufactures, sells, and services proprietary noninvasive monitoring, diagnostic, and therapeutic devices for cardiovascular disease, with engineering and production centered in its China-based facilities. VasoHealthcare has provided professional sales representation for General Electric Healthcare''s diagnostic imaging modalities since 2010, targeting independent hospitals, imaging centers, and multispecialty clinics across the continental United States. VasoTechnology delivers managed IT systems, healthcare software solutions, and secure network connectivity services for enterprise and clinical customers.

The company serves the healthcare sector''s middle market, including independent hospitals, imaging centers, and multispecialty clinics for imaging equipment sales, while its medical device unit reaches global markets through direct and partner channels. VasoTechnology supports enterprises and healthcare organizations with mission-critical applications, data storage, and security services.

Vaso Corporation emphasizes its cross-disciplinary expertise spanning medical devices, diagnostic imaging sales, and IT infrastructure, allowing it to address diverse clinical and enterprise needs.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Design of proprietary medical devices", "Manufacture of proprietary medical devices", "Sale and service of proprietary medical devices", "Professional sales representation for capital medical equipment", "Diagnostic imaging equipment sales", "Managed IT systems and services", "Healthcare software solutions", "Network connectivity services", "Engineering and production (China-based)", "Noninvasive cardiovascular monitoring, diagnosis, and treatment"], "industries": ["Healthcare", "Diagnostic imaging", "Cardiovascular medical devices", "Information technology", "Managed IT services", "Medical technology"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["GE Healthcare partnership for diagnostic imaging sales since 2010", "Proprietary noninvasive cardiovascular monitoring and therapeutic devices", "Engineering and production conducted in China-based facilities", "Managed IT systems, healthcare software, and network connectivity services", "Three distinct business units across healthcare and IT"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in Plainview, NY -> /", "Three business units: VasoMedical, VasoHealthcare, VasoTechnology -> /", "VasoMedical designs, manufactures, sells, services proprietary medical devices for noninvasive cardiovascular monitoring/diagnosis/treatment -> /", "Engineering and production mainly in China-based facilities (Wuxi) -> /", "VasoHealthcare provides professional sales representation for GE Healthcare diagnostic imaging since 2010 -> /", "VasoHealthcare serves independent hospitals, imaging centers, multispecialty clinics across continental US -> /", "VasoTechnology provides managed IT systems, healthcare software solutions, network connectivity services -> /", "Company formerly Vasomedical, Inc. -> /", "Public company with investor relations, SEC filings -> /", "Additional locations: Nashville, TN; Tampa, FL -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "VasoMedical for the design, manufacture, sale and service of proprietary medical devices; VasoHealthcare for professional sales services of diagnostic imaging equipment; and VasoTechnology for managed IT systems and services", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='vaso-medical-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Vaughan-Bassett Furniture has operated from Galax, Virginia, since its founding in 1919 by B.C. Vaughan and J.D. Bassett, Sr. What began as a small regional furniture company grew into the largest manufacturer of wooden adult bedroom furniture in the United States, remaining under the leadership of the Bassett family with John D. Bassett III serving as chairman.

The company employs more than 500 skilled artisans at its Galax factory, where they produce bedroom collections — including Dovetail, Tide & Timber, Cool Rustic, Bonanza, Pure Maple, and Maple Road — using wood solids and veneers such as oak, maple, cherry, ash, poplar, birch, beech, and pine. Modern manufacturing technology complements traditional craftsmanship, and the firm reports that 99 percent of its materials are sourced domestically.

Vaughan-Bassett sells through a dealer network to residential customers across the country. Its furniture is designed for real homes, meeting federal stability requirements under 16 CFR Part 1261 (ASTM F2057) for clothing storage units, and the company is a member of the American Home Furnishings Alliance.

The company''s differentiation rests on a deliberate choice to keep production in America when much of the industry moved overseas. That commitment is documented in the bestselling book Factory Man. Vaughan-Bassett also operates a One for One sustainability program that has contributed more than six million tree seedlings to the Virginia Department of Forestry, and it sources 99 percent of its lumber within 500 miles of its factories.', certifications=ARRAY['16 CFR Part 1261','ASTM F2057']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Solid wood furniture manufacturing", "Wood veneer processing", "Multi-finish application", "Furniture assembly", "Stability compliance testing (ASTM F2057)"], "industries": ["Residential furniture", "Home furnishings", "Wooden bedroom furniture"], "materials": ["Oak", "Maple", "Cherry", "Ash", "Poplar", "Birch", "Beech", "Pine", "Wood solids", "Wood veneers"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Largest U.S. manufacturer of wooden adult bedroom furniture", "Over 100 years of continuous manufacturing in Galax, Virginia", "99% of lumber sourced within 500 miles of the factory", "One for One program: 6+ million tree seedlings planted", "Furniture meets 16 CFR Part 1261 / ASTM F2057 stability standard"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1919 by B.C. Vaughan and J.D. Bassett, Sr. -> /about-us", "Largest manufacturer of wooden adult bedroom furniture in the U.S. -> /about-us", "Headquartered in Galax, Virginia -> /about-us", "More than 500 skilled artisans -> /about-us", "Bedroom collections: Dovetail, Tide & Timber, Cool Rustic, Bonanza, Pure Maple, Maple Road -> /", "Materials: oak, maple, cherry, ash, poplar, birch, beech, pine -> /about-us", "99% American materials, 99% lumber within 500 miles -> /about-us", "One for One program: 6+ million tree seedlings to Virginia Dept of Forestry -> /about-us", "Meets 16 CFR Part 1261 (ASTM F2057) stability standard -> /about-us", "Member of American Home Furnishings Alliance -> /about-us", "Factory Man book documents commitment to U.S. manufacturing -> /about-us"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Vaughan-Bassett has been making furniture in the foothills of the Blue Ridge Mountains in Galax, Virginia.", "founded_year": "1919", "employee_count": "500+", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='vaughan-bassett-furniture' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Vault Foods operates from its headquarters in Fair Oaks, Texas, with an SQF-certified treatment facility in Boerne, Texas. The company''s founding year and ownership structure are not publicly disclosed.

The company provides a food safety treatment service that uses an FDA-approved organic processing aid to reduce pathogens on foods such as nuts, seeds, and other packaged products. At its Boerne facility, the Neo-Pure system—developed in partnership with Agri-Neo—mists a proprietary biodegradable solution onto food surfaces and crevices, achieving a validated 5-log (≥99.999%) reduction of Salmonella, E. coli, and Listeria without heat, irradiation, or chemical gases. The process preserves the food''s raw taste, smell, texture, and nutrition, and the solution biodegrades completely, leaving no residue and requiring no label declaration.

Vault Foods serves food processors and manufacturers in the nut, seed, and packaged-food sectors who need to extend shelf life while maintaining a "truly raw" product claim. Its treatment is designed to integrate into existing supply chains, offering certified freshness without altering the natural qualities of the food.

The company emphasizes that its processing aid is so safe the FDA does not require labeling, and that the organic, biodegradable solution differentiates it from thermal or chemical alternatives. The service was created to give food brands a way to achieve high-level pathogen reduction while keeping products raw and organic-compliant.', certifications=ARRAY['SQF']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Food pathogen reduction treatment", "Organic processing aid application (misting)", "Neo-Pure system operation", "5-log reduction validation (Salmonella, E. coli, Listeria)", "SQF-certified food processing", "Biodegradable solution application", "Raw food preservation processing"], "industries": ["Food processing", "Nut and seed processing", "Packaged food manufacturing"], "materials": ["Nuts", "Seeds", "Packaged foods"], "equipment": ["Neo-Pure system"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "5-log (\u226599.999%) pathogen reduction", "built_on": ["FDA-approved processing aid with no labeling requirement", "Organic, biodegradable solution that leaves no residue", "Validated 5-log pathogen reduction without heat or irradiation", "Preserves raw taste, texture, and nutrition", "Integrates into existing supply chains via SQF-certified facility"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in Fair Oaks, Texas -> db", "SQF-certified treatment facility in Boerne, Texas -> /", "FDA-approved processing aid, no labeling required -> /", "Partners with Agri-Neo, uses Neo-Pure system -> /", "Validated 5-log (\u226599.999%) reduction of Salmonella, E. coli, Listeria -> /", "Process preserves natural taste, smell, texture, nutrition -> /", "Organic, biodegradable solution -> /", "Works with nuts, seeds, packaged foods -> /", "SQF certification -> db", "Technology for modern food industry -> /"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Your foods, including nuts and seeds, are transported to our SQF Certified treatment facility site locati