UPDATE companies SET description='Vermont Made Furniture Handcrafted by Thurston operates from a workshop in Brandon, Vermont. The company was founded in 1960 and remains family-owned and operated, now in its third generation of Thurston family leadership. What began as a local woodworking enterprise has grown into a direct-to-consumer maker of heirloom-quality solid wood furniture.

The company designs and builds bedroom, dining, office, and bath furniture from sustainably harvested North American hardwoods — primarily cherry, oak, walnut, and maple. Production runs from rough milling through finishing in their Vermont factory, with each piece made to order. Collections such as Amesbury, Manchester, Weybridge-Dover, Addison, Allen, Chelsea, and Armstrong span mid-century, Shaker, mission, and contemporary styles. Customers select wood species and configurations through a custom-order process; no inventory is held for immediate shipment.

The primary market is residential buyers furnishing homes across the United States. The company sells directly to consumers via its website, eliminating middlemen. It has served over 1,000 homes, shipping nationwide with free white-glove delivery on orders above $5,000.

Thurston emphasizes a lifetime guarantee on every piece, sustainable sourcing from well-managed forests, environmentally friendly finishes, and an energy-efficient workshop. The firm highlights its commitment to local employment — paying living wages to Vermont craftspeople in a safe workplace — and to reducing carbon emissions by manufacturing domestically rather than importing.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom solid wood furniture manufacturing", "Wood species selection (cherry, oak, walnut, maple)", "Rough milling to finishing", "Handcrafted joinery and assembly", "White-glove delivery service", "Furniture design and customization"], "industries": ["Residential furniture", "Home furnishings", "Interior design"], "materials": ["Cherry", "Oak", "Walnut", "Maple", "North American hardwoods"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Lifetime guarantee on every piece", "Handcrafted start to finish in Vermont factory", "Sustainable solid wood from well-managed North American forests", "Direct-to-consumer with no middleman", "Free nationwide white-glove delivery on orders over $5,000"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1960 -> db", "Brandon, Vermont location -> db", "Family-owned, three generations -> /", "Heirloom solid wood furniture -> /", "Custom wood selection: cherry, oak, walnut, maple -> /", "Lifetime guarantee -> /", "Handcrafted start to finish in factory -> /", "Sustainable practices: localized hardwoods, eco-friendly finishes, energy-efficient workshop -> /", "Made in America -> /", "Free white-glove delivery on $5000+ -> /", "Collections: Amesbury, Manchester, Weybridge-Dover, Addison, Allen, Chelsea, Armstrong -> /", "Furniture categories: bedroom, kitchen/dining, office/living, bath -> /", "Team of skilled Vermont craftspeople -> /", "Living wage, safe work environment -> /", "Served over 1,000 homes -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "From rough to refined, our solid wood furniture undergoes a meticulous furniture-making process, starting in the rough mill area of our factory and finishing in the wrapping area for direct shipment to you.", "founded_year": "1960", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": ["https://www.vermontmadefurniture.com/"], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='vermont-made-furniture-handcrafted-by-thurston' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Vermont Plastic Specialties, Inc. was founded in 1982 in Williston, Vermont. The company operates as a plastics fabrication and material supply business serving commercial and industrial customers across the Northeast.

The shop provides precision laser cutting, waterjet cutting, CNC routing, and custom fabrication for plastic, metal, and wood components. Its equipment includes a 4'' x 8'' waterjet, two lasers (4'' x 4'' and 4'' x 8''), a 4'' x 8'' CNC router, a horizontal panel saw capable of 10'' x 10'' sheets, and a diamond edge finisher for acrylic polishing. The company also maintains a large plastics inventory in thicknesses from 0.03 to 1 inch and offers material sales alongside fabrication services.

Customers include aerospace and industrial firms such as B.F. Goodrich, technology manufacturers like IBM Corporation, and construction-related businesses such as Engelberth Corporation. The company works with clients on projects ranging from museum-quality covers to point-of-purchase displays, providing free estimating and in-house consulting to solve application challenges.

