UPDATE companies SET description='Vesco Medical operates from New Albany, Ohio, in the Columbus metropolitan area. The company does not publicly state its founding year or ownership structure. Its leadership team includes President & CEO Tom Hancock, VP Global Business Development Derek O''Hara, VP Product Development & Innovation Dan Chirayath, Director of Operations & HR Michele Faith, VP of Sales Brian Grant, Director of Quality & Regulatory Assurance Garrett Noble, Controller Trisha Newcome, and National Accounts Director Steve Atkinson.

The company designs and manufactures enteral feeding devices, including feeding pumps with touch-screen controls, medicine bottle adapters in eight sizes, and a range of tube-feeding accessories. All products use ENFit connectors and are produced under an ISO 13485 certified quality management system with FDA 510(k) premarket clearance. The devices are made without natural rubber latex, DEHP, BPA, or other phthalate plasticizers. Vesco Medical does not disclose facility size, headcount, or production volumes.

Vesco Medical serves the medical device and healthcare industries, specifically enteral nutrition for patients from infants to aging adults. It is a member of the Global Enteral Device Supplier Association (GEDSA), which promotes international safety standards for tubing connectors.

Vesco Medical positions itself as the only enteral feeding device company that is exclusively ENFit-compliant, a differentiator it says reduces the risk of tubing misconnections. Its stated mission is to advance the quality of care and patient safety for those whose ability to consume nutrition is compromised. The company emphasizes continuous improvement through its ISO 13485 system, FDA good manufacturing practices, and 510(k) clearance.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 13485','FDA Registered','FDA 510(k) Premarket Clearance']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Enteral feeding device manufacturing", "ISO 13485 quality management", "FDA 510(k) regulatory clearance", "ENFit connector standardization", "Product development and innovation", "Regulatory and quality assurance", "Direct and distributor fulfillment"], "industries": ["Enteral feeding devices", "Medical devices", "Healthcare", "Enteral nutrition"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Only enteral feeding device company that is all ENFit all the time", "Products free of natural rubber latex, DEHP, BPA, and phthalate plasticizers", "ISO 13485 certified quality management system", "FDA 510(k) premarket clearance", "Member of Global Enteral Device Supplier Association (GEDSA)"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in New Albany, Ohio -> db", "Enteral feeding devices, medicine bottle adapters, feeding pumps -> /", "ISO 13485 Certified Quality Management System -> /about", "FDA Registered -> db", "FDA 510(k) Premarket Clearance -> /about", "Products made without natural rubber latex, DEHP, BPA, phthalates -> / and /about", "Exclusively ENFit-compliant products -> /about", "Member of Global Enteral Device Supplier Association (GEDSA) -> /about", "Leadership team: Tom Hancock (President & CEO), Derek O''Hara (VP Global Business Development), Dan Chirayath (VP Product Development & Innovation), Michele Faith (Director of Operations & HR), Brian Grant (VP of Sales), 