UPDATE companies SET description='Viking Steel Fabricators began in 1950 as the Fredericksburg Machine Shop in downtown Fredericksburg, Virginia. After moving to its current Airport Avenue location beside the city fairgrounds in the 1970s, the shop was purchased by Clayton Mills from his uncle Mr. Stoner. In 1985 Mills hired Don Breivik to start a steel fabrication division; Breivik bought the business in 1999, renaming it Fredericksburg Machine & Steel and expanding to 13 employees. Ownership passed to Don''s sons Luke and Erik in 2016, with Luke becoming sole owner in 2017. The 2019 acquisition of Virginia Architectural Metals added ornamental iron and historic restoration capabilities. The company remains family‑operated, with Luke Breivik as president and multiple relatives on staff.

The firm fabricates and erects structural and miscellaneous steel for commercial, institutional, and residential projects throughout Virginia, Washington, D.C., and Maryland. Services include shop and field welding, plate shearing, plate bending and rolling, pipe threading, plasma cutting, and custom handrails in carbon steel, aluminum, stainless steel, bronze, brass, and wrought iron. Viking also stocks steel shapes, plate, pipe, tubing, bar grating, and expanded metal for sale. A 13‑person crew works from the Airport Avenue facility, handling jobs from ornamental railings to large structural packages.

Completed projects span the Antietam Battlefield Tower (Maryland), the Admiral Club and the Pentagon (D.C. area), Virginia Railway Express stations, the Orange County Public Safety Building, the Eastern Shore Public Library, and a satellite dish mount in Greenland. Customers include general contractors, developers, government agencies, healthcare providers such as Patient First, and retailers like AAA. The historic preservation niche, strengthened by the Virginia Architectural Metals acquisition, targets restoration of landmark structures.

Viking highlights its 70‑plus years in Fredericksburg, mobile welding service, and a full steel inventory as differentiators. The 2019 closure of the machine shop to concentrate solely on fabrication reflects a strategic response to sustained demand for structural and ornamental metalwork, supported by the expertise of former Virginia Architectural Metals owners Mike and Betsy Rodrigue.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Structural steel fabrication", "Steel erection", "Welding (shop and field)", "Custom handrail fabrication", "Plate shearing", "Plate bending/rolling", "Pipe threading", "Plasma cutting", "Ornamental iron fabrication", "Historic preservation and restoration", "Steel material supply", "Maintenance and repair"], "industries": ["Commercial construction", "Government/Military", "Healthcare", "Education", "Public safety", "Historical preservation", "Residential", "Transportation", "Retail"], "materials": ["Carbon steel", "Aluminum", "Stainless steel", "Bronze", "Brass", "Wrought iron"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Serving the Fredericksburg area since 1950", "Mobile welding and repair service", "Large supply of steel shapes, plate, pipe, tubing, bar grating, and expanded metal", "Historic preservation and restoration expertise"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1950 -> db", "Headquarters Fredericksburg, VA -> db", "Employee count 13 -> db", "History: formerly Fredericksburg Machine Shop -> /", "Ownership transitions: Clayton Mills, Don Breivik, Luke Breivik -> /", "Services: steel fabrication & erection, welding, custom handrails, plate shearing, plate bending/rolling, pipe threading, plasma cutting, steel sales -> /", "Projects: Antietam Battlefield Tower, Admiral Club, The Pentagon, VRE, Orange County Public Safety Building, Eastern Shore Public Library, satellite dish mount Greenland -> /", "Materials: steel, aluminum, stainless steel, bronze, brass, wrought iron -> /", "Acquisition of Virginia Architectural Metals in 2019 -> /", "Family involvement (Luke Breivik owner, relatives working) -> /", "Mobile welding service -> /", "Large steel inventory -> /", "Historic preservation specialization -> /"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "We are a structural and misc steel fabricator.", "founded_year": "1950", "employee_count": "13", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='viking-steel-fabricators' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Viking Technology operates from a technology facility in Costa Mesa, California. The company has been delivering leading-edge design and engineering development in DRAM memory, Flash storage, and micro-packaging technologies for over two decades. No founding year or founders are disclosed in public materials.

The firm designs and manufactures ruggedized memory and storage solutions, including DDR4 multi-chip package modules, 2 TB M.2 PCIe NVMe drives, and persistent memory with integrated supercapacitors. Its capabilities span advanced testing in a clean room environment with 110 GHz validation, conformal coating, anti-sulfur resistor integration, and custom form-factor miniaturization. Production occurs at an ITAR-compliant, AS9100-certified U.S. facility, though headcount and floor space are not published.

Viking serves defense and aerospace programs, including ground, sea, and air platforms, as well as avionics and cockpit instrumentation. It also supplies automotive-grade memory rated for -40 °C to +105 °C, telecommunications infrastructure, and energy subsystem applications. Customers range from military prime contractors to industrial OEMs requiring extended temperature ranges from -55 °C to +125 °C.

The company emphasizes U.S.-based R&D, development, and production, coupled with long-standing strategic partnerships and comprehensive supply-chain management. Security features such as hardware AES 256-bit encryption, NSA 9-12 compliant write protection, and hardware-triggered quick erase are built into its military-optimized products.', certifications=ARRAY['AS9100','ITAR','ISO9001','ISO14001']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["DRAM memory design and manufacturing", "Flash storage design and manufacturing", "Micro-packaging technology", "Multi-chip package (MCP) assembly", "PCIe NVMe storage fabrication", "Persistent memory with integrated supercapacitor", "Ruggedization for extreme environments", "Miniaturization and custom form factor development", "Conformal coating", "Anti-sulfur resistor integration", "Wide operating temperature range qualification (-55\u00b0C to +125\u00b0C)", "Design validation and high-frequency testing (110 GHz)", "Clean room assembly and testing", "Custom product qualification", "Hardware AES 256-bit encryption implementation", "Hardware drive erase/sanitize", "Hardware write protection (including NSA 9-12, jumper triggered)", "USA-based R&D and development", "Supply chain management", "Automotive temperature rated memory production", "Military temperature rated memory production"], "industries": ["Telecommunications", "Defense/Aerospace", "Automotive", "Military/Defense (Ground, Sea, Air)", "Homeland Security", "Aerospace Avionics & Cockpit Instrumentation", "Energy Subsystems"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Designed and manufactured in the USA at an ITAR-compliant, AS9100-certified facility", "Operating temperature range from -55 \u00b0C to +125 \u00b0C for military grades", "Hardware-based AES 256-bit encryption and NSA 9-12 compliant write protection", "Advanced clean room testing with 110 GHz validation capability", "Conformal coating and anti-sulfur resistor components for harsh environments"], "facts_used": ["Location: Costa Mesa, California -> db", "Certifications: AS9100, ITAR, ISO9001, ISO14001 -> db", "Products: DDR4 MCP, 2TB M.2 PCIe NVMe, persistent memory with supercapacitor -> /", "Capabilities: conformal coating, anti-sulfur resistors, 110GHz testing, clean room -> /", "Industries served: defense/aerospace, automotive, telecommunications, homeland security, avionics, energy subsystems -> db", "Operating temperature ranges: -40\u00b0C to +85\u00b0C (Ind.), -40\u00b0C to +105\u00b0C (Auto), -55\u00b0C to +125\u00b0C (Mil) -> /", "Security features: hardware AES 256-bit encryption, NSA 9-12 write protect, quick erase -> /", "USA-based R&D, development, production -> /", "Strategic partnerships and supply chain management -> /", "Over two decades of experience -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Designed and manufactured in the USA at an ITAR compliant & AS9100-certified facility, Viking Technology Memory and Storage are high reliability solutions designed and optimized for Military & Aerospace applications", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": ["ITAR registered"], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='viking-technology' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Vintage Reclaimed Lumber Company was founded in 1999 in Oklahoma City, Oklahoma. The business began with a single storage building filled with wood salvaged from an old barn and has grown into a regional supplier of reclaimed lumber.

The company sources and sells a variety of reclaimed wood products including boxcar flooring from railcars, freightliner trailer flooring, live-edge slabs, beams, timbers, and barn wood planks. It also mills flooring and wall/ceiling products from laminated oak and other hardwoods, offers rough-sawn lumber, and provides finish products such as stains, waxes, and sealers. Inventory spans species like walnut, black oak, cottonwood, red oak, white oak, hemlock, and sycamore. The firm operates a warehouse where customers can select materials in person.

Customers include DIY enthusiasts, builders, tradesmen, architects, interior designers, decorators, and wholesalers across the United States. Affiliated companies—Grain & Grange Furniture Mfg and Old World Iron—extend the offering to custom furniture and decorative ironwork for builders and designers.

The company emphasizes its role in diverting historic lumber from landfills, noting it has sourced reclaimed wood since before the green movement gained popularity. It works with a network of pickers to recover ancillary items such as gears, pulleys, and tools from abandoned structures, incorporating them into furniture and architectural elements.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Reclaimed wood sourcing and salvaging", "Milling of flooring and wall/ceiling products", "Rough sawing", "Finish application (stains, waxes, sealers)", "Live-edge slab processing", "Warehousing and inventory selection", "Ancillary item sourcing (gears, pulleys, tools, containers)"], "industries": ["Construction", "Architecture", "Interior Design", "Wholesale Distribution", "DIY/Home Improvement", "Furniture Manufacturing"], "materials": ["Walnut", "Black Oak", "Cottonwood", "Red Oak", "White Oak", "Hemlock", "Sycamore", "Reclaimed Barn Wood", "Railcar Planks (Boxcar Wood)", "Semi-Trailer Flooring (Freightliner Wood)", "Live-Edge Slabs", "Laminated Oak Hardwoods"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Sources reclaimed lumber from historic barns, railcars, and semi-trailers nationwide", "Mills flooring and wall/ceiling products from reclaimed hardwoods", "Offers a range of finish products including stains, waxes, and sealers", "Maintains a warehouse for in-person material selection", "Affiliated with custom furniture and decorative iron fabrication shops"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1999 -> pages:/", "Headquarters Oklahoma City, Oklahoma -> db", "Started from a single storage building with salvaged barn wood -> pages:/", "Sources boxcar wood, freightliner wood, live-edge wood, beams, timbers, barn wood planks -> pages:/", "Mills flooring and wall/ceiling products from laminated oak and other hardwoods -> pages:/", "Offers rough sawn wood, stains, waxes, sealers -> pages:/", "Inventory includes walnut, black oak, cottonwood, red oak, white oak, hemlock, sycamore -> pages:/", "Serves DIYers, builders, tradesmen, architects, decorators, designers, wholesalers nationwide -> pages:/", "Affiliated with Grain & Grange Furniture Mfg and Old World Iron -> pages:/", "Emphasizes diverting historic lumber from landfills, sourcing before green movement -> pages:/", "Works with pickers to source ancillary items (gears, pulleys, tools, containers) -> pages:/", "Operates a warehouse for customer selection -> pages:/"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "flooring and wall/ceiling products milled from laminated oak and other hardwoods", "founded_year": "1999", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='vintage-reclaimed-lumber-company' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Virginia Electric Supply was founded in 1980 in Duffield, Virginia, initially focusing on distributing specialty fasteners to the underground mining market.

Over the decades, the distributor expanded its portfolio to include electrical, data communications, maintenance/repair/operating (MRO), and electrical OEM products. Today it operates as a single-source procurement partner, offering coordinated supply of distribution and control equipment, lamps and lighting, ballasts, circuit breakers, fittings, conduit, wire and cable, and industrial supplies. The firm employs 19 full-time distribution professionals with a combined 460 years of industry experience.

Virginia Electric Supply serves commercial, industrial, government, mining, and utility sectors, as well as telecommunications and natural gas extraction markets. Its customer base ranges from manufacturing and process plants to electrical contractors, investor-owned utilities, municipalities, and rural electric cooperatives. The company provides value engineering, sourcing, on-site materials management, design assistance, and project management services tailored to each segment.

