UPDATE companies SET description='Warrior Energy, LLC was established in 2019 in Devils Lake, North Dakota, as a Native American–owned, SBA-certified small disadvantaged business. The company operates as a limited liability company and has expanded to include a branch in Grand Forks. Leadership includes President/COO Scott Schmaltz and General Manager/CEO Darin Hultberg, among a team of project managers and trade foremen.

The firm provides multi-discipline general contracting and program management, self-performing electrical construction (high/low voltage wiring, cable tray, switchgear, fiber optics), instrumentation and control services (calibration, loop checks, PLC/DCS panel installation), HVAC maintenance and controls, welding fabrication (structural stands, skids, platforms), roustabout and pipeline services (facility construction, flowline excavation, welding, backfill), insulation (fiberglass, jacketing, removable blankets), and coating/painting. Bonding capacity is $500,000 per project with a $1,000,000 aggregate.

Warrior Energy serves industrial, government, oilfield/energy, institutional, commercial, and municipal facility owners. Typical projects include new construction, retrofits, emergency repairs, and planned maintenance for clients such as energy producers, public agencies, and commercial developers.

The company emphasizes a full-service approach that covers pre-construction planning, design, engineering, coordination, and project management, backed by 24-hour emergency response. Its core values—service, quality, and integrity—are framed around adaptability, attention to detail, and transparent accountability.', certifications=ARRAY['SBA Targeted Small Business','Certified Small Disadvantaged Business','100% Native American Owned']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["General Construction", "Construction Management", "Design/Build Solutions", "Contract Consulting", "Electrical Construction", "Instrument Control Services", "Control Panel & Automation", "HVAC Services & Maintenance", "Welding Fabrication", "Roustabout and Pipeline Services", "Insulation Services", "Coating and Painting"], "industries": ["Industrial", "Government", "Oilfield/Energy", "Institutional", "Commercial", "Municipal"], "materials": ["High Performance Fiberglass Insulation", "Galvalume PLUS AZ-60 Jacketing Sheeting"], "equipment": ["Programmable Logic Controllers (PLC)", "Distributed Control Systems (DCS)", "Marshalling Cabinets", "HMI Enclosures", "Insulated Enclosures"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["24-hour emergency service availability", "Full-service scope from pre-construction planning through project management", "Native American\u2013owned, SBA-certified small disadvantaged business", "Bonding capacity of $500K single project / $1M aggregate", "Multi-discipline self-perform capabilities across electrical, instrumentation, HVAC, welding, and pipeline"], "facts_used": ["Founded 2019 -> /about", "Headquarters Devils Lake, ND -> /about", "Native American owned, SBA Small Business, Certified Small Disadvantaged Business -> /about", "Services: general contracting, electrical, instrumentation, HVAC, welding, pipeline, insulation -> /services", "Industries: industrial, government, oilfield/energy, institutional, commercial, municipal -> /about", "Certifications: SBA Targeted Small Business, Certified Small Disadvantaged Business, 100% Native American Owned -> /about", "CAGE code 8K9E3 -> /about", "Bonding capacity $500K single/$1M aggregate -> /about", "Leadership team names (Schmaltz, Hultberg, etc.) -> /about", "24-hour emergency service -> /about", "Full-service pre-construction to project management -> /about", "LinkedIn URL -> db"], "company_type": "Installer / service company", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Warrior Energy, LLC (WEL) specializes in general contracting program management services, electrical installations, instrumentation and controls installations, and related services for industrial, government, oilfield/energy, institutional, commercial, and municipal facility projects.", "founded_year": "2019", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "8K9E3", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": ["https://www.linkedin.com/company/warriorenergyllc/"], "ownership_tags": ["Small business"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='warrior-energy' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Watersong Custom Furniture operates from Albuquerque, New Mexico, where owner Andy has run the business as a sole proprietor for over four decades. Andy’s woodworking roots trace back to childhood in Africa, where he observed utilitarian woodcraft, and later in Italy, where he encountered elaborate carved furniture. Those experiences shaped a philosophy that values quality, craftsmanship, and durability. The shop has remained at the same location since its inception, a 1,500‑square‑foot space divided between a small showroom and a working area with a finishing booth.

The company produces one‑of‑a‑kind residential furniture including tables, entertainment centers, headboards, beds, dressers, display cases, desks, bookshelves, cabinetry, benches, and vanities. Every piece is designed and built by Andy alone, from hand‑selecting lumber to final delivery. He works primarily in domestic hardwoods such as ash, cherry, hickory, maple, oak, pine, poplar, and walnut, supplemented by exotic species like purple heart, padauk, zebra wood, wenge, and mahogany for accents. Joinery is screwed and glued rather than stapled, and hardware consists of European hinges and steel ball‑bearing slides. A water‑based finish option is available for environmentally sensitive clients.

Watersong serves homeowners and individual clients seeking custom pieces that fit unique spaces and functional needs. Examples from the portfolio include a low maple table for a meditation room, a built‑in vanity with dual sinks and a cedar‑lined hamper, and entertainment centers designed to adapt to evolving technology.

Andy emphasizes that the sole‑proprietor model ensures a single point of accountability from design through delivery, eliminating the “too many cooks” problem. The company’s differentiators are its four‑decade tenure at one address, hand‑selected materials, premium hardware, and a willingness to ship finished pieces across the country—from Wyoming to Texas and California to New Jersey.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom furniture design", "Woodworking", "Joinery (screwed and glued)", "Finishing (water-based)", "Hardware installation (European hinges, ball-bearing slides)", "Custom cabinetry", "Built-in furniture", "Free-standing furniture", "Custom beds", "Headboards", "Entertainment centers", "Desks", "Bookshelves", "Display cases", "Benches", "Vanities"], "industries": ["Custom furniture", "Residential furniture"], "materials": ["Ash", "Cherry", "Hickory", "Maple", "Oak", "Pine", "Poplar", "Walnut", "Purple Heart", "Padauk", "Zebra Wood", "Wenge", "Mahogany", "Alder", "Veneer core plywood", "Melamine"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "4 to 8 weeks typical; some pieces within a week", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Sole proprietor handling design through delivery", "Hand-selected lumber and veneer\u2011core plywood", "European hinges and steel ball\u2011bearing slides", "Screwed\u2011and\u2011glued joinery, no staples", "Water\u2011based finish option", "Over 40 years at the same Albuquerque location", "Nationwide delivery capability"], "facts_used": ["Location: Albuquerque, NM -> db", "Owner: Andy -> /about", "Business tenure: over 40 years -> /", "Shop size: 1500 sq ft -> /about", "Sole proprietor -> /about", "Materials: domestic hardwoods (ash, cherry, hickory, maple, oak, pine, poplar, walnut) and exotic woods (purple heart, padauk, zebra wood, wenge, mahogany) -> /about", "Plywood: veneer core, melamine -> /about", "Hardware: European hinges, steel ball-bearing slides -> /about", "Joinery: screwed and glued -> /about", "Finish: water-based option -> /about", "Lead time: 4-8 weeks typical, some within a week -> /about", "Delivery: in-town and out-of-town (multiple states) -> /about", "Product examples: tables, entertainment centers, headboards, beds, dressers, display cases, desks, bookshelves, cabinetry, benches, vanities -> /", "Custom design tailored to exact needs -> /", "Albuquerque the Magazine feature Feb 2023 -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "For over four decades now, I''ve been making quality custom furniture right here in Albuquerque.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "1", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='watersong-custom-furniture' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Waxoyl USA operates from Westford, Vermont, where it was founded in 1971. The company specializes in corrosion protection solutions for transportation, machinery, and structures, drawing on more than five decades of experience in the field.

The product line centers on three main coatings: Hardwax, a tough, flexible wax-based barrier for underbody protection; Professional 120-4, a cavity fogging treatment that penetrates seams and displaces moisture; and Hardwax21, formulated for maximum abrasion resistance in extreme environments. All products are supplied in kegs, tins, and aerosol cans alongside a range of professional application tools designed to reach cavities without drilling.

The coatings are used by original equipment manufacturers across automotive, commercial vehicle, and rail sectors, including car, bus, and truck makers, vehicle importers, pre-delivery inspection centers, train builders, and heavy earth-moving equipment producers. Specialists worldwide apply the system to protect bridges, fleet vehicles, and industrial structures.

Waxoyl emphasizes that a single application of 120-4 can protect for the life of a vehicle, with active protection spanning -40°F to 300°F. The coatings are safe on paint, rubber, and electrical components, and they stop existing surface rust while lubricating moving parts such as window tracks. Touch-ups are needed only where the coating has been physically abraded.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Corrosion protection coating", "Cavity fogging", "Underbody coating", "Rust inhibition", "Customized corrosion solutions", "Application tool supply", "Crystal Coating Sheet"], "industries": ["Automotive", "Commercial vehicles", "Rail", "Heavy equipment", "Industrial machinery", "Structures"], "materials": ["Metal substrates"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["360\u00b0 corrosion protection for underbody and cavities", "Single application of 120-4 protects for the life of the vehicle", "Active protection from -40\u00b0F to 300\u00b0F", "Safe on paint, rubber, electrical components, and lubricates window tracks", "Application tools reach cavities without drilling"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1971 -> db", "Headquarters Westford, Vermont -> db", "More than 55 years experience -> /", "Hardwax, Professional 120-4, Hardwax21 products -> /", "Industries served: car, bus, truck, train, heavy equipment manufacturers -> /", "Temperature range -40\u00b0F to 300\u00b0F -> /", "Safe on paint, rubber, electrical components -> /", "Application tools snake through existing drains without drilling -> /", "One application protects for life of vehicle -> /", "Waxoyl kills existing surface rust -> /", "Products available in kegs, tins, aerosol cans -> /", "Customized solutions for transportation, machinery, structures -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Waxoyl Professional makes customized solutions to retain value and the like-new qualities of all types of transportation, machinery and structures.", "founded_year": "1971", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='waxoyl-usa' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Weavetec, Inc. was founded in 1987 by the Pennington family in Blacksburg, South Carolina, in the Upstate region. The company remains family-owned and managed, drawing on over 90 years of textile industry experience across generations. Harold Pennington Jr. serves as vice president, while Andrew Pennington oversees sales and operations, and Laurinda Pennington manages customer service.

The firm operates as a specialty weaver producing custom woven fabrics for industrial and home furnishing markets. Its capabilities include sectional warping on Benninger warpers, dobby weaving on looms of varying widths and harness counts, and jacquard weaving configured around a standard 54‑inch width. In‑house throw finishing provides washing, drying, cutting, folding, and sewing for blankets and tapestries. The plant employs approximately 200 people.

Weavetec serves the upholstery fabric industry, manufacturers of woven throws and tapestry blankets, and broader industrial textile applications. Customers range from brands seeking multicolor tapestry blankets to companies needing durable upholstery materials and specialty fabrics for niche uses.

The company emphasizes construction flexibility, a reputation for responsive customer service, and product value, all framed by a mission to produce Made‑in‑USA textiles with integrity and precision.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Sectional warping", "Dobby weaving", "Jacquard weaving", "Throw finishing (washing, drying, cutting, folding, sewing)", "Custom woven fabrics", "Woven throw and tapestry blankets", "Upholstery fabrics"], "industries": ["Industrial fabrics", "Home furnishing", "Upholstery", "Textile manufacturing"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Benninger sectional warpers", "Dobby looms", "Jacquard looms (54-inch width)"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Family-owned and managed since 1987", "In-house finishing (washing, drying, cutting, folding, sewing)", "Construction flexibility across warp and weave configurations", "Made-in-USA manufacturing with a focus on integrity and precision", "Exceptional customer service reputation"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1987 in Blacksburg, SC -> db", "Family-owned and managed by Pennington family -> db, /", "Employee count 200 -> db", "Processes: sectional warping, dobby weaving, jacquard weaving, throw finishing -> /", "Equipment: Benninger sectional warpers, dobby looms, jacquard looms -> /", "Products: custom woven fabrics, woven throw and tapestry blankets, upholstery fabrics -> /", "Industries: industrial & home furnishing, upholstery fabric industry -> /", "Mission: glorify Jesus Christ, Made in USA, integrity, innovation, precision -> /about", "Management team names (Harold Pennington Jr., Andrew Pennington, Laurinda Pennington, etc.) -> /about", "Construction flexibility, customer service reputation, product value -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Weavetec, Inc. is a specialty weaver owned and managed by the Pennington family that has operated in Upstate South Carolina since 1987.", "founded_year": "1987", "employee_count": "200", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='weavetec-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Weber Auto & Truck Parts, Inc. has operated as a family-owned auto salvage and parts business in Derry, New Hampshire since 1966. Now in its second generation, the company sits on more than 10 acres near the intersection of Interstate 93 and Route 28, serving customers six days a week.

The yard stocks foreign and domestic used auto parts managed through a computerized inventory system, and also buys scrap metal and non‑ferrous materials. In addition to parts sales, Weber Auto offers junk‑vehicle removal any day of the week, sells used batteries with a core‑exchange program, and carries used tires and rims priced by tread depth.

The business is open to the general public and advertises top‑dollar payment for junk cars and scrap metal, positioning it as both a retail parts outlet and a recycling collector for the southern New Hampshire region.

