UPDATE companies SET description='White Lightning Aviation Ground Power is based in Lexington, Kentucky. The company traces its roots to the 1980s when founder Jon Sisk, a longtime pilot, began building high-current DC power supplies for mobile electronics demonstrations. Recognizing a need for reliable, affordable ground power units in general aviation, Sisk and his engineering team developed the first Enhanced Flight GPU, establishing the company''s focus on airframe ground power.

The company designs and manufactures a line of ground power units (GPUs) covering 14 V, 28 V, and dual‑voltage configurations, including smart GPUs with integrated battery‑maintenance chargers. It also produces aviation‑grade power cables, wiring harnesses, and plug assemblies, and distributes the BatteryMINDer® line of charger‑maintainers. All manufacturing is done in the United States, with product models such as the M2875‑114 (114 A, 28 V), M2827 (27 A, 24/28 V), M1428‑DV (dual‑voltage mini), M2850 (50 A, 28 V), and several 14 V variants for certified and experimental aircraft.

Its equipment is used to power cockpit avionics — such as Garmin G1000 suites — during preflight, maintenance, database updates, and training without draining the aircraft battery. Customers include owners of certified aircraft like the Cessna Skylane and Piper Navajo, as well as experimental/amateur‑build operators.

The company was started because Jon Sisk saw a gap in affordable, reliable hangar ground power. It differentiates itself by pursuing three principles: sensibly designed, well‑made products at reasonable prices; great customer service with direct phone support; and manufacturing everything possible in the USA.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Ground power unit design and manufacturing", "Battery maintenance charger integration", "Aviation cable and wiring harness assembly", "BatteryMINDer\u00ae product distribution", "Technical support and documentation", "Firmware development for GPU products", "GPU electrical calculation tool", "FAA\u2011certified aircraft wiring kit installation support"], "industries": ["General aviation", "Business aviation", "Flight training", "Aircraft maintenance", "Experimental/amateur\u2011built aircraft", "Certified aircraft (FAA Part 23/25)"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Manufacturing everything possible in the USA", "Great customer service with direct phone support", "Sensibly designed, well\u2011made products at reasonable prices", "Compact, rugged GPUs with versatile features for pilots", "Distribution of aviation\u2011specific BatteryMINDer\u00ae chargers"], "facts_used": ["Lexington, Kentucky headquarters -> db", "Jon Sisk, owner and CEO -> homepage (/) ", "Continuous involvement in general aviation since 1980 -> db description and homepage (/) ", "Manufactures ground power units (GPUs) for 14V, 28V, dual voltage -> homepage (/) product listings", "Distributes BatteryMINDer\u00ae chargers -> db description and homepage (/) ", "Provides wiring kits for FAA\u2011certified aircraft -> db description", "Three company goals: sensibly designed products, great customer service, US manufacturing -> homepage (/) ", "Product models: M2875\u2011114, M2827, M1428\u2011DV, M2850, M1435\u2011EXP, M1435, M1435P -> homepage (/) ", "Serves general aviation, business aviation, experimental, certified aircraft -> homepage (/) and db industries_served", "Customer testimonials from Cessna Skylane and Navajo owners -> homepage (/) "], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "His engineers designed and built the first Enhanced Flight GPU. Manufacturing everything possible here in the USA.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='white-lightning-aviation-ground-power' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Whiteside Manufacturing Co. was founded in 1954 in Delaware, Ohio, when the company''s patriarch used $800 earned from officiating high school basketball to start a business in a two-car garage. What began as a family operation—run by the founder, his mother, and his wife—has grown into a second-generation, family-owned manufacturer of professional-grade garage equipment.

The company produces mechanic''s creepers, creeper seats, industrial-grade platforms, storage solutions, and specialty garage equipment, along with a full line of replacement parts. Operating from more than 100,000 square feet of manufacturing space, Whiteside holds nearly 100 patents and serves a global customer base with products made in the USA. Its catalog includes dozens of SKUs such as the Over-the-Engine Creeper, adjustable rider creepers, convertible creeper-seats, and padded shop seats.

Whiteside''s equipment is used across automotive, heavy-duty, big-truck, industrial, agriculture, refinery, and aerospace sectors. The company has earned multiple "Vendor of the Year" awards from customers for innovation, service, and delivery performance. It also offers custom garage equipment designed to match specific industry standards and requirements.

The founder''s original mission—to build the finest garage equipment in the professional tool world—remains the guiding principle. The leadership team, led by CEO Kirt Whiteside and CFO Terry Whiteside, continues to operate on the credo: build it better, build it right, and never settle.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Creeper manufacturing", "Creeper seat manufacturing", "Garage equipment manufacturing (platforms, storage, specialty equipment)", "Replacement parts production", "Custom equipment design and manufacturing", "Patent development and intellectual property protection"], "industries": ["Automotive", "Heavy-duty", "Big-truck", "Industrial", "Agriculture", "Refineries", "Aerospace"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Made in USA manufacturing", "Nearly 100 patents protecting product designs", "Over 100,000 sq ft manufacturing facility", "Family-owned, second-generation leadership", "Custom garage equipment design and manufacturing"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1954 -> /about-us", "Founded with $800 start by father officiating high school basketball -> /about-us", "Started in two-car garage -> /about-us", "Over 100,000 sq ft manufacturing space -> /about-us", "Industries served: automotive, heavy-duty, big-truck, industrial, agriculture, refineries, aerospace -> /about-us", "Nearly 100 patents -> /about-us", "Second generation leadership: Terry Whiteside (CFO), Kirt Whiteside (CEO) -> /about-us", "Products: creepers, creeper seats, garage equipment, replacement parts -> /about-us and /", "Custom garage equipment design -> /", "Made in USA -> /about-us", "Vendor of the Year awards -> /about-us", "Headquarters: Delaware, Ohio -> db", "Family-owned -> /about-us"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "America''s Leading Manufacturer of Mechanic''s Creepers, Seats and More!", "founded_year": "1954", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "